      "text": [
        " : كَانَ مَعِي جِرَابَانِ مِنْ مِسْكٍ أَحَدُهُمَا رَطْبٌ وَ اَلْآخَرُ يَابِسٌ فَبَدَأْتُ بِالرَّطْبِ فَبِعْتُهُ ثُمَّ أَخَذْتُ اَلْيَابِسَ أَبِيعُهُ فَإِذَا أَنَا لاَ أُعْطَى بِالْيَابِسِ اَلثَّمَنَ اَلَّذِي يَسْوَى وَ لاَ يَزِيدُونِّي عَلَى ثَمَنِ اَلرَّطْبِ فَسَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ أَ يَصْلُحُ لِي أَنْ أُنَدِّيَهُ قَالَ \"لاَ إِلاَّ أَنْ تُعْلِمَهُمْ\" قَالَ فَنَدَّيْتُهُ ثُمَّ أَعْلَمْتُهُمْ قَالَ \"لاَ بَأْسَ بِهِ إِذَا أَعْلَمْتَهُمْ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3839 - It is narrated from Dawood bin Sirhan, from Abu Abdillah (as), who said:\nI had two sacks of musk-one was moist, and the other was dry. I started with the moist one and sold it.\nThen I took the dry one to sell, but I found that I was not offered the price it was worth, and they would not pay me more than the price of the moist musk.\nSo I asked Imam (as) about that, whether it was permissible for me to mix them.\nImam (as) said: \"No, unless you inform them.\"\nHe said: \"So I mixed them and then informed them.\"\nImam (as) said: \"There is no harm in it if you inform them.\""
        ]
      }
    },
